From: RT3000 developers <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: reserve headroom for empty aligned RX buffers

The RX refill and monitor-status paths allocate empty skbs, then call
skb_pull() to align skb->data. skb_pull() cannot advance an empty skb, so
the requested alignment is not applied. Use skb_reserve() at these two
allocation sites; keep skb_pull() semantics for populated skbs unchanged.

Also report monitor-status descriptor/cb DMA address mismatches immediately
before DMA sync. This diagnostic does not change ownership or control flow.

Offline validation: both allocation sites use dev_alloc_skb() before the
alignment adjustment. The monitor-status path takes descriptor paddr and
cookie from the same ring entry, while skb paddr comes from its IDR entry.
This candidate does not establish the panic root cause. The skb alignment
change follows the upstream discussion at
https://lore-kernel.gnuweeb.org/ath11k/20260719215817.2468580-3-wabsie%40gmail.com/T/
and https://github.com/eisbaw/ath11k-page-frag-fix . No device validation is
claimed.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -411,8 +411,8 @@ int ath11k_dp_rxbufs_replenish(struct ath11k_base *ab, int mac_id,
 		if (!IS_ALIGNED((unsigned long)skb->data,
 				DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE)) {
-			skb_pull(skb,
-				 PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
-				 skb->data);
+			skb_reserve(skb,
+				    PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
+				    skb->data);
 		}
 
 		paddr = dma_map_single(ab->dev, skb->data,
@@ -3720,7 +3720,7 @@ static struct sk_buff *ath11k_dp_rx_alloc_mon_status_buf(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	if (!IS_ALIGNED((unsigned long)skb->data,
 			DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE)) {
-		skb_pull(skb, PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
-			 skb->data);
+		skb_reserve(skb, PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
+			    skb->data);
 	}
 
 	paddr = dma_map_single(ab->dev, skb->data,
@@ -3951,6 +3951,15 @@ static int ath11k_dp_rx_reap_mon_status_ring(struct ath11k_base *ab, int mac_id,
 
 			rxcb = ATH11K_SKB_RXCB(skb);
 
+			if (unlikely(!rxcb->paddr || paddr != rxcb->paddr))
+				dev_warn_ratelimited(ab->dev,
+					"mon status DMA mismatch mac_id=%d srng_id=%d ring_id=%u "
+					"cookie=0x%x buf_id=%d desc_paddr=%pad cb_paddr=%pad "
+					"skb=%p len=%u tailroom=%u\n",
+					mac_id, srng_id, srng->ring_id, cookie, buf_id,
+					&paddr, &rxcb->paddr, skb, skb->len,
+					skb_tailroom(skb));
+
 			dma_sync_single_for_cpu(ab->dev, rxcb->paddr,
 						skb->len + skb_tailroom(skb),
 						DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
